  "accepted_conclusions": [
    {
      "conclusion_id": "cancel-then-verify-reclamation",
      "title": "Separate request cancellation from reclamation of resources still in use",
      "claims": [
        "At the pinned vLLM revision, finish_requests removes valid requests from scheduling queues, sets terminal status, and calls _free_request. Remote-KV receive state and connector return values can delay _free_blocks. _free_blocks calls _free_request_blocks, which either frees immediately or queues blocks behind a processed-step fence; update_from_output advances that fence before draining deferred frees.",
        "At the pinned SGLang revision, abort_request records an in-flight chunked request for later handling, removes waiting requests directly, and marks running requests via to_finish. Its host-staged decode branch preserves the destination and prepares abort instead of invoking receiver.abort on that branch. The code and comments do not establish immediate termination of every already-launched device operation.",
        "At the pinned TGI v3 revision, the response channel is attached to a queued Entry. In the inspected prefill path, client.prefill returns before send_responses observes channel closure and filter_send_generations removes entries; filter_batch then updates or clears the next cached batch. This is not a pre-forward cancellation acknowledgement."
      ],
      "diagnostic_use": "Trace the concrete request state, ownership release, delayed-free queue or next-batch filtering separately; retain pending state until its own completion condition is observed.",
